CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight
SCALE_REALISM: Holds for the measured workload: real C4 multilingual validation text, 20,000 docs across 5 languages, 9,044 model-identical NFKC-twin pairs, residual_FN_rate 95.1%, and 34.6% of residual FNs still missed under production-like 5-gram char-shingle MinHash at T=0.8. Main gap: L1 measures generated NFKC twins from real documents, not observed duplicate-pair frequency in a full crawl; artifact should expose exact scripts, HF dataset revisions, and tokenizer-normalizer assumptions for reproduction.
RATIONALE: v001. I find no fatal prior-art collision: shipping dedup systems found either use weaker/default text normalization in the dedup path (datatrove simplify_text: lower + NFD strip accents; NeMo Curator: char n-gram MinHash on text field) or only provide tokenizer-side NFKC machinery (SentencePiece/HF tokenizers). The result clears the committee#1 gate by a large margin: 95.1% residual false negatives versus >=1% GREEN threshold, with every language above 55.6%. The fix is simple engineering, but the contribution is the measured cross-system failure mode and its scale under real multilingual web characters, not the act of adding unicodedata.normalize("NFKC").
